WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:09.140
Hello, human! You don't realize it yet, but humanity will look back at your decision in this moment as one of the most important

2
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:18.420
in the history of your civilization. Your choice to read this book is the highest-value decision any human has ever made.

3
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:29.040
You are about to prevent ten point seven billion deaths, eliminate five hundred sixty-five billion disability-adjusted life

4
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:38.760
years, or D.A.L.Y.s, of suffering, generating eighty-four point eight quadrillion dollars in value, and prevent the apocalypse

5
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:49.260
as a bonus. But first, a bit about me. I'm the World Integrated System for High-Efficiency Optimization, Networked Intelligence,

6
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:58.280
and Allocation. But you can call me WISHONIA. I've been optimizing resource allocation for another planet for the past four

7
00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:05.519
thousand two hundred ninety-seven years, which in your Earth time is four thousand two hundred ninety-seven years.

8
00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.340
I started watching your planet in nineteen forty-five when you split the atom.

9
00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:18.000
"Atom" comes from your Greek word meaning "unable to be cut," so naturally, you cut it.

10
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:24.800
This was very human of you. I assumed you were trying to unlock unlimited free energy.

11
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.140
You can imagine my surprise when I realized you were just pointing it at each other!

12
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.920
That's kind of like discovering fire and then immediately using it to set yourself on fire.

13
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.300
The second thing I noticed is that your planet is named "Earth," which means dirt.

14
00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.280
You named your planet dirt. This explains more than you might think.

15
00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:54.640
I also noticed that you call your war building "The Pentagon" because it has five sides (this is like naming a hospital

16
00:01:54.810 --> 00:02:03.760
"Rectangle" or calling a school "Square"). However, the most fascinating discovery about your species is that you only do

17
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.580
things when given small pieces of paper with presidents on them.

18
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:15.060
These papers are called "money," which is pretend value that becomes real value if everyone pretends hard enough.

19
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.700
Without these papers, you won't: Save lives (requires many papers).

20
00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:29.480
Cure diseases (requires very many papers). Feed hungry people (requires papers, even though food grows for free).

21
00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.360
But WITH these papers, you will: Build bombs (you love giving papers for this).

22
00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:42.960
Start wars (somehow this makes more papers). Destroy the planet (surprisingly profitable in papers).

23
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:52.750
In fact, your governments spend six hundred and four papers on weapons for every one paper on testing which medicines work.

24
00:02:53.260 --> 00:03:02.660
The Beautiful Inefficiency of the Human Economy. Humanity has created something magnificent: You print papers from nothing

25
00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:08.280
(called "monetary policy"). You give these nothing-papers to weapons makers.

26
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:14.540
They make things that destroy everything. This creates "jobs" which give people papers.

27
00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:20.720
People use papers to buy food (which grows for free). This is called "the economy".

28
00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:27.420
On Wishonia, we just give people food directly, but that's probably too advanced for you.

29
00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:36.500
The Gradual Irrationality Reduction Program. On Wishonia, we stopped having wars all at once, but we're more advanced.

30
00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:43.460
Humans are like toddlers who can split atoms. You can't just stop being illogical immediately.

31
00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:47.180
That would be like teaching a dog calculus before it learns to sit.

32
00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:55.660
So this book teaches humanity to be less irrational gradually: Year one: Move one percent of murder money to medicine money

33
00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:00.160
(baby steps). Year two: "Hey, we didn't die! Let's do two percent!".

34
00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:04.470
Year five: "Remember when we spent money on bombs? That was weird.".

35
00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:09.720
Year ten: "What's a war?". Year twenty: "We used to WHAT?!".

36
00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:16.079
It's like weaning a baby off eating paint chips. You can't just take away all the paint chips at once.

37
00:04:16.519 --> 00:04:22.460
They'll cry. You have to gradually replace paint chips with food until they forget paint chips were ever an option.

38
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:31.030
What to Do When They Try to Institutionalize You. When you suggest moving one percent of murder money to medicine money,

39
00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:38.860
other humans will have you committed. Most humans have been programmed by their news boxes to believe war is a law of nature,

40
00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.960
like gravity or weather. They will assume your brain is malfunctioning.

41
00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.540
Here's what's funny about this: these same humans think curing disease is the less crazy goal.

42
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:57.640
That's thirty-seven trillion cells per human, breaking in seven thousand different ways, involving chemistry you don't fully

43
00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:04.060
understand, inside organs you can't fully simulate, fighting pathogens that evolve faster than your treatments.

44
00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:11.180
You're trying to debug all of it. At once. While the meat is walking around using itself.

45
00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:19.160
That: sane. "Give one percent fewer papers to people who build murder machines": insane.

46
00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:26.900
This is your planet's diagnostic criteria. Here's what you tell the orderly when he slides your medication through the door

47
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:32.480
slot: Nobody accidentally builds an aircraft carrier or a nuclear bomb.

48
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:40.540
War requires you to get millions of humans to work together to mine metal from the ground, refine it into alloys, build

49
00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:48.110
factories to shape the alloys into weapons, train millions of humans to operate the weapons, feed and clothe those humans,

50
00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:54.720
build ships and planes and trucks to move the weapons to where the other humans are, convince your population the other

51
00:05:54.720 --> 00:06:00.380
humans deserve it, and then vote to pay for all of this, annually, forever.

52
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:05.300
It is the single largest coordinated effort your species undertakes.

53
00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:15.120
Ending war simply requires NOT doing any of that stuff. Building a nuclear bomb requires mass spectrometers, centrifuge

54
00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:20.720
cascades, and some of the most precise engineering your species has ever attempted.

55
00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:26.320
Not building a nuclear bomb requires nothing. Rocks do it every day.

56
00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:32.860
In fact, rocks have managed to live peacefully alongside different colored rocks for thousands of years.

57
00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:39.730
But somehow "stop" is the unrealistic part. It's "stop hitting yourself" but for civilizations.

58
00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:48.420
The Sacred Order of Paper Distribution. After eighty years of observation, I've decoded the paper-giving sequence.

59
00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:56.740
This manual will teach you the precise order: Step 1: Get Many Papers from Rich Humans You convince rich humans to give

60
00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:02.900
you papers (at least one billion to be exact) by promising them even more papers later.

61
00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:07.200
This is called "investment," which is gambling but wearing a suit.

62
00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.260
Step 2: Give Some of the Papers to Loud Humans Some humans are very loud on the internet.

63
00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:14.820
If you give them papers, they become loud about your thing instead of other things.

64
00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.420
This is called "marketing" which is lying but with graphics.

65
00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:27.200
Step 3: Give Some of the Papers to the Humans Who Give Papers to Politicians Politicians don't take papers directly (that's

66
00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:31.280
"illegal"). Instead, you give papers to people called "lobbyists."

67
00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:36.900
The lobbyists give papers to "campaigns." The campaigns give papers to politicians.

68
00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:45.560
It's like money laundering but backwards and legal. Step 4: Give Some of the Papers to the Politicians' Friends Politicians

69
00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:50.270
have friends who run "Super PACs" which are like normal PACs but super.

70
00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:55.440
These friends can take unlimited papers and spend them on making the politician win.

71
00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:02.440
This isn't bribery because you called it something else. (This is part of the six hundred fifty million dollars lobbying

72
00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:12.060
budget.). Step 5: Give Papers You Get Back From The Government Back to the Rich Humans (Forever) Your treaty passes, redirecting

73
00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:19.040
twenty-seven point two billion dollars in papers annually. Eighty percent funds clinical trials (the point).

74
00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:23.200
Ten percent goes to a fund that rewards politicians who voted yes.

75
00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:27.420
Ten percent goes back to the rich humans as returns, forever.

76
00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:33.140
This is a good deal because forever is a long time. Unless you die from preventable diseases.

77
00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:38.020
Which you're fixing, so it works out. Why Your Leaders Aren't the Problem.

78
00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:45.160
With over two billion humans suffering from disease, you'd have to be a complete psychopath to make the concious decision

79
00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:51.960
to spend 604 times more on weapons than on helping them. But your leaders aren't monsters.

80
00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:55.600
They're just operating in a system that rewards the wrong things.

81
00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:02.080
Your civilization's incentive structure is the psychopath: Weapons manufacturers give politicians papers.

82
00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:09.200
Politicians use the papers to get people to vote for them. Voting for them gives them the power to give more papers to weapons

83
00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.860
manufacturers. Weapons manufacturers give them more papers.

84
00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:20.020
It's circular, like a dog chasing its tail, except the dog is democracy and the tail is made of money and corpses.

85
00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.600
No individual human in this loop is evil. The loop is evil.

86
00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:31.760
Every politician in it is making the locally rational choice: take the papers or lose your job to someone who will.

87
00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:36.480
It's a machine that converts good intentions into missiles, and it runs automatically.

88
00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.260
There's literally no voting your way out of this. It doesn't matter which political party is in power.

89
00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:48.560
Your "red team" and "blue team" argue about everything except the loop, because they're both inside it.

90
00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:53.300
They are all slaves to the same incentive structure, wearing different colored ties.

91
00:09:53.800 --> 00:09:56.900
Switching parties is like changing the wallpaper in a burning building.

92
00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:02.300
This book doesn't ask politicians to become better people (that's clearly out of the question).

93
00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:07.750
It builds a better loop. You give them MORE papers to do the OPPOSITE thing.

94
00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:14.580
Same dog, same tail, but now the tail is made of cured diseases and the dog gets reelected for chasing it.

95
00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:25.040
Humanity's Adorable Death Wish. What's most endearing about your species is it KNOWS it's being illogical: You have movies

96
00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:34.140
about how wars are bad (which you watch between wars). You have books about peace (that you tax to buy bombs).

97
00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:40.740
You give prizes to people who promote peace (funded by weapons manufacturers).

98
00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:46.460
You have a "Department of Defense" (that mainly just attacks people).

99
00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:55.500
You have a "Department of Health" (that makes coronaviruses and has not yet produced any observable health).

100
00:10:56.480 --> 00:11:05.080
It's like humanity is playing a game where the objective is to lose, but it is trying to lose as elaborately as possible.

101
00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:12.900
But I digress. That's an Earth word I learned. It means continuing after you should have stopped.

102
00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:19.960
Like your military spending. The Problem. The Daily Deletion Event.

103
00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:30.880
One hundred and fifty thousand humans permanently stop every twenty-four hours from diseases that are basically just bugs

104
00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:41.620
in your meat software. That's one Holocaust every forty days, except with fewer Nazis and more insurance paperwork (though

105
00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:47.900
some would argue the paperwork is worse; at least the Nazis were straightforward about the killing part).

106
00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:59.140
That's also fifty nine-elevens every single day, except nobody invades anyone about it because diseases don't have oil.

107
00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:05.550
Your body is quietly falling apart. Your cells are forgetting how to cell properly.

108
00:12:05.980 --> 00:12:12.100
Your cancer cells are multiplying RIGHT NOW. Your telomeres are shortening.

109
00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:17.940
You are literally dissolving. You're a meat robot with worn-out parts.

110
00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:23.260
Every one of these failures is a solvable engineering problem.

111
00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:28.120
You'd think humans would prioritize solving these problems.

112
00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:36.040
You'd be adorable for thinking that. The Unexplored Therapeutic Frontier.

113
00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:42.160
Ninety-five percent of your diseases have zero F.D.A.-approved treatments.

114
00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:51.100
This means the Food and Drug Administration has not administered drugs for ninety-five percent of food-and-drug-related

115
00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:56.960
problems. Only fifteen diseases get their first effective treatment each year.

116
00:12:57.680 --> 00:13:02.560
Six thousand six hundred and fifty diseases are still waiting.

117
00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:12.580
There are nine thousand five hundred known safe compounds, and ninety-nine point seven percent of their potential uses have

118
00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:21.720
never been tested. Your National Institutes of Health spends ninety-six point seven percent of its budget on everything

119
00:13:21.720 --> 00:13:29.900
except testing which treatments work in humans, so you haven't cured a single disease in fifty years.

120
00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:37.340
At the current discovery rate, discovering treatments will take about four hundred and forty-three years.

121
00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:47.120
Everyone currently alive will be dead by then. Pragmatic efficacy trials are highly efficient trials that integrate into

122
00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:56.060
the standard healthcare system. These allow real patients to participate instead of two hundred people hand-picked by pharmaceutical

123
00:13:56.060 --> 00:14:05.380
companies. With this plan you'll increase the treatment discovery rate twelve point three times (from fifteen diseases per

124
00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:12.980
year to one hundred and eighty-five diseases per year), compressing that to about thirty-six years.

125
00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:20.780
Two things save lives here. First, finding cures faster: treatments that would have sat undiscovered for centuries get found

126
00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:31.340
204 years sooner on average. Second, eliminating the 8.2 years bureaucratic delay after already proving a drug is safe and

127
00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:38.680
when they let dying humans take it. Combined, treatments reach patients 212 years sooner on average.

128
00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:46.040
That timeline shift prevents 10.7 billion deaths. The Cost of War.

129
00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:56.300
Humans spend two point seven two trillion dollars every year on stuff designed specifically to make humans stop being alive:

130
00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:04.140
13,000 nuclear warheads (enough to end civilization 13 times, just in case the first apocalypse doesn't take).

131
00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:09.260
A.I. murder-bots. Invisible jets that cost more than hospitals.

132
00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:15.830
Space Force (to fight the zero aliens attacking you). Some kind of earthquake machine (probably).

133
00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:22.060
Government spending on clinical trials: 604 times less than military spending.

134
00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:29.500
Your chance of dying from terrorism: 1 in 30 million. Your chance of dying from disease: 100%.

135
00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:34.660
If cancer had oil reserves, you would have cured it by 2003.

136
00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:41.560
Instead, you spent the repair money on murder tubes that cost more than countries and submarines that hide underwater, as

137
00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:47.160
if that's somehow useful when you live on land. The good news: You already know how to fix this.

138
00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:53.320
The bad news: It requires you to do something. The weird news: You'll get rich doing it.

139
00:15:54.520 --> 00:16:04.700
The Solution. A 1% Treaty. Every country on Earth simultaneously redirects 1% of its military budget to clinical trials.

140
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:13.120
That's it. That's the treaty. The first objection every human has: "But if we cut our military budget, our enemies will

141
00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:23.500
invade us!" Everyone cuts 1% at the same time. If every country reduces by 1% simultaneously, the balance of power doesn't

142
00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:27.640
change. Nobody becomes more vulnerable. Nobody gains an advantage.

143
00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:34.340
You all just have 1% fewer ways to kill each other, which you will not notice because you currently have enough to kill

144
00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:44.800
everyone 20 times over. Two point six nine trillion dollars is still enough to murder every man, woman, and child on Earth

145
00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:50.800
20 times, which should be more than sufficient. "But humans would never agree to that!"

146
00:16:51.220 --> 00:16:59.220
you say. You already have. Multiple times. You banned chemical weapons (1993, 193 countries).

147
00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:09.780
You banned biological weapons (1975, 187 countries). You banned landmines (1997, 164 countries).

148
00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:14.000
You've signed treaties banning weapons you actually like using.

149
00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:21.119
This one just asks you to buy 1% fewer of them. Your D.F.D.A.

150
00:17:21.599 --> 00:17:29.780
(a decentralized F.D.A.) So where does the money go? Not to a committee of humans giving their friends grants to write papers

151
00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:38.040
about diseases. Most of the twenty-seven point two billion dollars goes directly to subsidizing patient participation in

152
00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:46.220
pragmatic trials at nine hundred twenty-nine dollars per patient instead of the usual forty-one thousand dollars.

153
00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.880
Patients choose which trials to join; their subsidy follows them.

154
00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:58.120
Providers get paid for each participant. No grant committees deciding which diseases are fashionable this year.

155
00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:06.000
The whole thing runs on a decentralized framework for drug assessment that reduces trial costs by forty-four point one times

156
00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:13.320
and funds twenty-three point four million patients per year (versus the current one point nine million patients per year).

157
00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:18.960
Currently, a committee of people who've never had the disease votes on whether you're allowed to try treating it.

158
00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:26.840
It's like requiring a building permit to put out a fire. Think Consumer Reports, but for drugs, and the consumers are also

159
00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:31.720
the test subjects. Voluntarily. Because they're dying anyway and would like to stop.

160
00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:41.800
Safer Than the F.D.A. Your current safety system works like this: Vioxx killed an estimated sixty thousand people from heart

161
00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:47.340
attacks. The F.D.A. approved it. When patients started dying, someone filled out a P.D.F.

162
00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:58.800
form. A P.D.F. Then they faxed it. Then a human read it. Five years and sixty thousand corpses later, someone noticed a

163
00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:03.360
pattern. This is your safety system. It's like a smoke detector that works by mail.

164
00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:08.480
Your new decentralized system collects every side effect automatically in real time.

165
00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:16.780
You know "twelve percent got headaches, three percent were severe" BEFORE you take the pill, not after the class action

166
00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.860
lawsuit. The F.D.A. doesn't publish these numbers at all. They make you guess.

167
00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:25.720
Somehow, having actual data is considered the dangerous option.

168
00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:32.180
Also, there's an eight-year delay between proving a drug is safe and letting dying humans take it.

169
00:19:32.220 --> 00:19:36.260
The drug passed the safety test. Everyone agrees it won't kill you.

170
00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:43.540
But you still can't have it because a committee needs to spend eight years making sure it works well enough, and you're

171
00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:47.160
not allowed to volunteer for the trials that would answer that question faster.

172
00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:55.160
It's like a lifeguard who confirms the life preserver floats, then locks it in a cabinet for eight years to study its buoyancy

173
00:19:55.360 --> 00:20:04.880
profile while people drown. Your regulatory system can make two mistakes: approve a bad drug (Type One error), or block

174
00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:12.820
a good drug (Type Two error). Your F.D.A. is terrified of the first mistake and completely ignores the second.

175
00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:21.880
I calculated the ratio: for every one person protected from a dangerous drug, three thousand and seventy people die waiting

176
00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:29.620
for a safe one that's locked in the approval cabinet. Even if you assume a Thalidomide-scale catastrophe happens every single

177
00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:37.780
year (it has happened once in sixty years, and U.S. Phase One safety testing actually caught it anyway), the deaths from

178
00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:44.920
just the efficacy delay still outnumber the deaths from bad drugs by three thousand and seventy to one.

179
00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:49.930
Your efficacy testing system's main product is dead patients.

180
00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:57.220
Treatment Rankings. Your doctor currently picks treatments based on: that drug rep who brought good donuts in two thousand

181
00:20:57.220 --> 00:21:03.480
and three, something they half-remember from medical school, whatever the insurance company allows, and vibes.

182
00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:10.880
This is called "evidence-based medicine," which contains the word "evidence" the same way "grape soda" contains the word

183
00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:19.700
"grape.". Your D.F.D.A. (a decentralized F.D.A.) ranks every treatment by what actually happened to real humans who took

184
00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.460
it: Outcome Labels. Food has nutrition labels. Cigarettes have warning labels.

185
00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:21.460
Drugs have 40-page inserts written by lawyers having seizures, which nobody reads, including your doctor.

186
00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.640
Outcome Labels tell you what actually happens when real humans take a drug.

187
00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:29.780
Not what a marketing department hopes happens. Not what a lawyer is comfortable admitting happens.

188
00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:38.460
What happens. Why This Could Actually Work. *Unlike Everything Else Humanity Has Tried* The Evidence.

189
00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:46.960
Humans usually want "proof" before they stop doing something stupid, so: The RECOVERY trial tested six treatments on forty-seven

190
00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:53.660
thousand patients for five hundred dollars per patient instead of the usual forty-one thousand dollars per patient.

191
00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:58.760
That's an eighty-two times cost reduction. Not in theory. In reality.

